        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Michael Herz, Lloyd Kaufman, Roland Emmerich\n- Companies: Troma Entertainment, Centropolis Entertainment\n- Products: The Toxic Avenger series, Tromeo and Juliet, The Noah's Ark Principle\n- Topics: independent film studios, comedic horror films\n\nFacts:\n- In 1984, Roland Emmerich began his work in the film industry by directing The Noah's Ark Principle as part of his university thesis.\n- In 1985, Roland Emmerich co-founded Centropolis Entertainment with his sister.\n- Michael Herz and Lloyd Kaufman are the co-founders of Troma Entertainment.\n- Troma Entertainment is described as the world's longest-running independent film studio.\n- Troma Entertainment is known for comedic horror films including The Toxic Avenger series and Tromeo and Juliet.",
